{
  "unit": {
    "id": "es-a2-u12",
    "title": "Future tense",
    "subtitle": "The futuro simple: hablaré, comeré, viviré",
    "level": "A2",
    "order": 12,
    "xp_reward": 20
  },
  "grammar": {
    "title": "Talking about tomorrow",
    "intro": "The <b>futuro simple</b> is one of the easiest tenses in Spanish: take the <b>whole infinitive</b> and add one set of endings — the <b>same endings for -ar, -er and -ir verbs</b>. <i>Mañana hablaré con ella</i> (Tomorrow I'll talk to her). Watch the accents, and learn a handful of irregular stems.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "tag": "formación",
        "heading": "Infinitive + endings",
        "body": "Keep the full infinitive and add: <b>-é, -ás, -á, -emos, -éis, -án</b>. No dropping the -ar/-er/-ir — the ending sticks straight onto it:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "yo",
            "hablaré"
          ],
          [
            "tú",
            "hablarás"
          ],
          [
            "él/ella",
            "hablará"
          ],
          [
            "nosotros",
            "hablaremos"
          ],
          [
            "vosotros",
            "hablaréis"
          ],
          [
            "ellos",
            "hablarán"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "Mañana <b>hablaré</b> con ella.",
            "en": "Tomorrow I'll talk to her.",
            "note": "hablar + é"
          },
          {
            "es": "<b>Comeremos</b> a las ocho.",
            "en": "We'll eat at eight.",
            "note": "comer + emos"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "acentos",
        "heading": "Mind the accent",
        "body": "Every form except <b>nosotros</b> carries a written accent. Forgetting it changes the meaning — <b>hablare</b> (no accent) is a different, rare form, while <b>hablaré</b> is \"I will speak\".",
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>Viviré</b> en Madrid.",
            "en": "I'll live in Madrid.",
            "note": "accent on the é"
          },
          {
            "es": "Ellos <b>comprarán</b> la casa.",
            "en": "They'll buy the house.",
            "note": "accent on the á"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "irregulares",
        "heading": "Irregular stems (same endings!)",
        "body": "A few common verbs change the <b>stem</b>, but the endings stay identical. Learn the stem and you know all six forms:",
        "conj": [
          [
            "tener",
            "tendré"
          ],
          [
            "hacer",
            "haré"
          ],
          [
            "poder",
            "podré"
          ],
          [
            "salir",
            "saldré"
          ],
          [
            "venir",
            "vendré"
          ],
          [
            "poner",
            "pondré"
          ],
          [
            "decir",
            "diré"
          ]
        ],
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>Tendré</b> tiempo mañana.",
            "en": "I'll have time tomorrow.",
            "note": "tener → tendr-"
          },
          {
            "es": "<b>Haré</b> la cena esta noche.",
            "en": "I'll make dinner tonight.",
            "note": "hacer → har-"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "tag": "tiempo",
        "heading": "Time markers",
        "body": "The future often pairs with words that point ahead: <b>mañana</b> (tomorrow), <b>la próxima semana</b> (next week), <b>el año que viene</b> (next year).",
        "ex": [
          {
            "es": "<b>La próxima semana</b> viajaré a Roma.",
            "en": "Next week I'll travel to Rome.",
            "note": "la próxima semana"
          },
          {
            "es": "<b>Mañana</b> saldremos temprano.",
            "en": "Tomorrow we'll leave early.",
            "note": "salir → saldr-"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "takeaways": [
      "Future = full infinitive + é, ás, á, emos, éis, án (same for all verbs).",
      "Every form except nosotros has a written accent: hablaré, hablarás, hablará, hablaréis, hablarán.",
      "Irregular stems keep the same endings: tendré, haré, podré, saldré, vendré, pondré, diré.",
      "Pair it with mañana, la próxima semana, el año que viene."
    ],
    "mistakes": [
      {
        "w": "Mañana hablare con ella.",
        "r": "Mañana hablaré con ella.",
        "why": "The yo form needs the accent: hablaré, not hablare."
      },
      {
        "w": "Mañana teneré tiempo.",
        "r": "Mañana tendré tiempo.",
        "why": "tener has an irregular stem: tendré, not 'teneré'."
      },
      {
        "w": "Comerémos a las ocho.",
        "r": "Comeremos a las ocho.",
        "why": "The nosotros form has no accent: comeremos."
      }
    ]
  },
